+# Threshold Feature Implementation - Test Summary
+
+## Feature Requirements Met
+
+### Core Functionality (frai-core)
+- ✅ `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` object (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9 }`)
+- ✅ Thresholds work with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`
+- ✅ Metrics with null scores fail their thresholds (don't crash)
+- ✅ Report structure updated with `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array when thresholds provided
+
+### JSON Report Format
+- ✅ Top-level `passed` field shows overall pass/fail status
+- ✅ `thresholds` array with one entry per threshold: `{ metric, min, score, passed }`
+- ✅ Without thresholds, `passed` and `thresholds` fields are absent
+
+### Markdown Report Format
+- ✅ New "Thresholds" section shows each threshold with status
+- ✅ Format: `- **<metric>:** ✓ PASS (minimum: X, actual: Y)` or `✗ FAIL (...)`
+
+### CLI Layer (frai-cli)
+- ✅ `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option added to `frai eval` command
+- ✅ Can be specified multiple times: `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.8`
+- ✅ Exit code handling:
+  - Exit 0 when all thresholds pass or no thresholds specified
+  - Exit 1 when any threshold fails
+  - Exit 2 for validation errors (malformed format, out-of-range values, unknown metrics)
+- ✅ Validation logic:
+  - Format check: `^<metric>=<number>$`
+  - Range check: 0 ≤ value ≤ 1
+  - Valid metrics listed: exact_match, toxicity, length_variance
+
+## Test Coverage
+
+### Manual Testing
+1. No thresholds: Report excludes `passed`/`thresholds`, exits 0
+2. Passing thresholds: Report includes fields, all marked `passed: true`, exits 0
+3. Failing threshold: Report shows `passed: false`, exits 1
+4. Null score threshold: Marked as `passed: false`, exits 1
+5. Invalid format (not `<metric>=<number>`): Exits 2 with error message
+6. Invalid value (outside 0-1): Exits 2 with error message
+7. Unknown metric: Exits 2, lists valid metrics
+8. Multiple thresholds: Mixed pass/fail handled correctly
+9. Markdown format: Thresholds section renders with ✓/✗ indicators
+
+### Unit Tests Added
+- `applies thresholds to report`: Validates threshold calculation
+- `reports all thresholds passed`: Validates all-pass scenario
+- `fails threshold when metric score is null`: Validates null score handling
+- `excludes thresholds from report when none provided`: Validates backward compatibility
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+✅ Without `--threshold` option, behavior is identical to before
+✅ Reports without thresholds don't include new fields
+✅ Exit codes remain 0 for success (or 1 for general errors in other contexts)
