 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Thresholds (Gate on Metrics)
+- `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` object (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.95 }`).
+- Thresholds enable CI gates: `frai eval` exits 0 if all thresholds pass, 1 if any fails.
+- Each threshold specifies a metric ID and minimum required score (0–1 range).
+- Metrics with null scores (e.g., exact match without references) fail their thresholds.
+- CLI `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (can be repeated for multiple thresholds); exits 2 on validation errors (unknown metrics, out-of-range values, malformed format).
+- JSON reports gain top-level `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array when thresholds are provided.
+- Markdown reports gain a "Thresholds" section showing PASS/FAIL status per threshold.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
+- Thresholds work with custom metrics via the `thresholds` parameter to `generateReport`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
